{"id": "sevt_01AQngPbJUYyccN3B4tQFLzR", "content": [{"text": "**Timeline**\n- Checkout deployed `de6541f` at 14:38:10. Checkout p99 went from about 78 ms at 14:37 to 2201 ms at 14:38 and about 4000 ms by 14:40. It stayed at 4\u20134.8 s through 14:59.\n- The inventory deploy `a9efec4` (catalog cache disabled) landed at 14:39:40. That is after the spike began, so it can't be the trigger. It may add some load, but I didn't check inventory metrics.\n\n**Diff (`de6541f`, \"refactor for readability\")**\n- It replaces one batched `order_id IN (...)` query on `OrderItem` with a per-order query inside a loop. This is an N+1 pattern, and it's the first item on the runbook's list.\n\n**Log confirmation**\n- Before the deploy, checkout logs show only the batched `WHERE order_id IN (?)` query.\n- The per-row `WHERE order_id = ?` query first appears at 14:38:22, about 12 s after the deploy. There are 2448 of them through 14:59:59.\n\n**Root cause:** `de6541f` \u2014 the \"readability\" refactor turned the single batched order_items query into one query per order row (N+1), which is what pushed checkout p99 from about 80 ms to about 4 s. Reverting it should fix the spike.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:42:20.182750Z", "type": "agent.message"}
